From: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gps: propagate MT6685 clock selector read errors

The clock query initializes value to zero and ignores the regmap_read()
result, turning a bus error into a valid 26 MHz result. Return the error
instead. The existing ioctl returns the helper result directly, so no UAPI
number, layout or success enum changes. Keep missing-regmap behavior.
Normalize this source file's CRLF endings before applying this patch.

Signed-off-by: xxxvik-xakerxxx <19531907+xxxvik-xakerxxx@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/connectivity/gps/data_link/linux/gps_dl_linux_clock_mng.c b/connectivity/gps/data_link/linux/gps_dl_linux_clock_mng.c
--- a/connectivity/gps/data_link/linux/gps_dl_linux_clock_mng.c
+++ b/connectivity/gps/data_link/linux/gps_dl_linux_clock_mng.c
@@ -99,8 +99,8 @@
 int gps_dl_clock_mng_get_platform_clock(void)
 {
 	struct regmap *map = gps_dl_clock_mng_get_regmap();
-	int value = 0;
+	unsigned int value;
 	int retval = 0;
 
 	if (!map) {
 		GDL_LOGE("failed to get regmap.\n");
@@ -108,7 +108,11 @@
 	}
 
-	regmap_read(map, DCXO_DIGCLK_ELR, &value);
+	retval = regmap_read(map, DCXO_DIGCLK_ELR, &value);
+	if (retval) {
+		GDL_LOGE("failed to read platform clock: %d\n", retval);
+		return retval;
+	}
 	if (value & 0x1)
 		retval = 1; /*52M*/
 	else
 		retval = 0; /*26M*/
